LEARNER: Why does easing make it feel less robotic?
MENTOR: Things in the real world speed up and slow down gradually, so a move at one constant speed that starts and stops instantly reads as machine-made. Easing adds that gradual speed-up and slow-down, and your eye takes it as weight and intent.

